usage: zc emit <src> [flags]
Emit standalone C17 to -o FILE (or stdout). The runtime is inlined,
so the single .c needs no extra include paths.
--mark-natives writes a comment line before each piece of C a unit's
nativec.zd rendered, naming the row and the file and line it is written
at; without those lines the C is the same.
--line-marks writes `#line` directives naming the source file and line
each statement's and each function's C came from, so a tool that reads C
positions (a coverage counter, a debugger) reports zerolang ones; without
those lines the C is the same.
It takes the flags of build, without --save-temps.
